WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.520
This is The Spread, your energy
markets briefing for Friday,

2
00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:05.520
the twenty-seventh of November.

3
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:08.560
This episode is written and read with AI.

4
00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:12.480
Yemen's Houthis have struck Saudi
Arabia's Red Sea ports of Jeddah and

5
00:00:12.560 --> 00:00:16.880
Jazan. That puts the kingdom's route
around Hormuz in the line of fire,

6
00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:20.640
and Brent has climbed back toward
ninety-six dollars as supply fears

7
00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:23.200
push aside this month's talk of a surplus.

8
00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:27.280
On the markets. January Brent traded
at ninety-five dollars ninety at

9
00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:31.600
noon Eastern time on Thursday, up
one point three percent on the day.

10
00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:35.040
That's up from a close of
eighty-nine dollars forty on Monday.

11
00:00:35.120 --> 00:00:38.160
West Texas Intermediate was at
eighty-four dollars seventy,

12
00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:41.200
after touching seventy-nine
dollars ten earlier in the week,

13
00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:43.440
all according to OilPrice dot com.

14
00:00:43.520 --> 00:00:48.040
In Europe, gas storage was sixty-seven
point two percent full as of Wednesday,

15
00:00:48.080 --> 00:00:50.427
according to Gas Infrastructure Europe.

16
00:00:50.533 --> 00:00:53.867
Turning to the Red Sea. The
Houthis hit Jeddah and Jazan,

17
00:00:53.893 --> 00:00:57.547
and the exchange of fire with Saudi
Arabia shows no sign of easing,

18
00:00:57.573 --> 00:01:01.520
Rigzone reported. This comes after
Wednesday's attack on Ras Tanura on

19
00:01:01.560 --> 00:01:05.413
the Gulf coast. The Houthis now
say that strike caused fires,

20
00:01:05.467 --> 00:01:08.120
while Saudi Arabia had said
the drones were intercepted,

21
00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:10.080
according to OilPrice dot com.

22
00:01:10.160 --> 00:01:13.080
No damage has been reported
at either coast so far.

23
00:01:13.120 --> 00:01:16.640
A statement from Saudi Arabia or
Aramco on loadings would show whether

24
00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:19.573
exports were touched. Prices moved anyway,

25
00:01:19.627 --> 00:01:23.040
and Standard Chartered argues the
market now needs a fresh shock to fall

26
00:01:23.120 --> 00:01:26.267
further. That's the bank's
view, not a consensus.

27
00:01:26.293 --> 00:01:30.080
The Red Sea coast matters because
it's Saudi Arabia's bypass for barrels

28
00:01:30.120 --> 00:01:32.120
that would otherwise go through Hormuz.

29
00:01:32.160 --> 00:01:35.760
With its ports under attack, that
outlet is now exposed alongside the

30
00:01:35.800 --> 00:01:39.440
Gulf. Charterers lifting from the
Red Sea could face higher war-risk

31
00:01:39.520 --> 00:01:41.000
premiums as a result.

32
00:01:41.040 --> 00:01:44.640
Over in the Gulf itself, tanker
traffic through Hormuz has picked up

33
00:01:44.720 --> 00:01:46.480
even as the violence has grown.

34
00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:49.333
According to Vortexa data
reported by Bloomberg,

35
00:01:49.387 --> 00:01:53.440
the seven-day average of crude, fuel
and liquefied natural gas tankers

36
00:01:53.480 --> 00:01:56.360
was above twenty-six a day
for most of this month.

37
00:01:56.400 --> 00:01:59.240
That ran from the first to
the nineteenth of November.

38
00:01:59.280 --> 00:02:02.720
Earlier in the war it was below
twenty-five on at least two-thirds of

39
00:02:02.800 --> 00:02:06.640
days. All this came while attacks and
mine incidents were at their highest

40
00:02:06.680 --> 00:02:09.000
of the war, according to gCaptain.

41
00:02:09.040 --> 00:02:12.880
Iran's Islamic Revolutionary Guard
Corps Navy says a liquefied natural

42
00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:15.320
gas carrier hit a mine and exploded.

43
00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:18.800
It claims the ship had switched off
its tracking and used a route Tehran

44
00:02:18.920 --> 00:02:21.760
considers illegal. The
ship hasn't been named,

45
00:02:21.840 --> 00:02:23.760
and the claim is unconfirmed.

46
00:02:23.800 --> 00:02:26.880
There's more detail on the restriction
from the Abu Dhabi National Oil

47
00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:31.920
Company. A Petroleum Ports Authority
notice bars tankers carrying crude,

48
00:02:32.160 --> 00:02:36.160
products, liquefied gases and chemicals
from moving near the main export

49
00:02:36.240 --> 00:02:39.360
facilities, Splash
twenty-four seven reported.

50
00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:43.280
Meanwhile, commentators close to the
Guard Corps are pushing for a declared

51
00:02:43.360 --> 00:02:46.400
tanker convoy to sail
through the US blockade.

52
00:02:46.480 --> 00:02:49.680
They pair that with threats against
Gulf neighbours' oil infrastructure

53
00:02:49.840 --> 00:02:54.400
if US forces fire on Iranian ships,
according to OilPrice dot com.

54
00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:58.320
The same reporting projects Iran's
crude and condensate revenue reaching

55
00:02:58.480 --> 00:03:03.240
zero by mid-December. This is
advocacy, not a government decision.

56
00:03:03.520 --> 00:03:07.280
Kpler's note from the nineteenth
of November saw signs Iran may test

57
00:03:07.320 --> 00:03:11.120
the blockade with small tankers,
but no breakout in exports.

58
00:03:11.600 --> 00:03:16.480
On corporate deals, a US-led group has
signed for Lukoil's foreign business.

59
00:03:16.560 --> 00:03:20.640
A consortium led by Eldridge, which
includes the US International Development

60
00:03:20.720 --> 00:03:24.440
Finance Corporation, has agreed
to buy Lukoil International,

61
00:03:24.480 --> 00:03:29.040
according to World Oil. Until
Thursday this rested on press reports.

62
00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:31.320
Now the buyers have
announced it themselves,

63
00:03:31.360 --> 00:03:34.667
Rigzone reported, though
there's no word from Lukoil.

64
00:03:34.693 --> 00:03:38.000
The portfolio covers about three
hundred and fifty thousand barrels of

65
00:03:38.080 --> 00:03:40.293
oil equivalent a day of production.

66
00:03:40.347 --> 00:03:44.360
That's spread across eleven countries,
plus three European refineries.

67
00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:47.680
It's a share swap, and it still needs
approval from the Treasury's Office

68
00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:49.480
of Foreign Assets Control.

69
00:03:49.520 --> 00:03:53.360
If it closes, those refineries move
from sanctioned Russian ownership

70
00:03:53.520 --> 00:03:55.760
into US-allied hands.

71
00:03:55.880 --> 00:03:59.733
Turning to gas, Europe's storage
draw is quickening in the cold.

72
00:03:59.787 --> 00:04:03.040
The daily withdrawal on Wednesday
was point six three of a percentage

73
00:04:03.120 --> 00:04:05.720
point, according to Gas
Infrastructure Europe.

74
00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:08.160
On Monday it was point five zero.

75
00:04:08.200 --> 00:04:11.840
Dutch network operator Gasunie wants
the Netherlands to build a strategic

76
00:04:11.920 --> 00:04:15.400
gas reserve, though it says
there's no immediate shortage risk,

77
00:04:15.440 --> 00:04:17.333
OilPrice dot com reported.

78
00:04:17.387 --> 00:04:21.360
In Britain, the National Energy System
Operator flagged a margin shortfall

79
00:04:21.440 --> 00:04:25.480
of more than two point seven gigawatts
for Thursday afternoon and evening.

80
00:04:25.520 --> 00:04:29.240
That was the third tight day in
a row for the UK power system.

81
00:04:29.280 --> 00:04:31.467
Some relief may come from Egypt.

82
00:04:31.493 --> 00:04:35.440
A liquefied natural gas carrier off
Idku points to a possible restart

83
00:04:35.520 --> 00:04:39.160
of exports after a nine-month
pause, according to Kpler.

84
00:04:39.200 --> 00:04:40.440
A few more things.

85
00:04:40.480 --> 00:04:44.320
Two delegates say OPEC plus is
weighing a rollover of current quotas

86
00:04:44.440 --> 00:04:47.600
into January, citing
uncertainty from the Iran war,

87
00:04:47.680 --> 00:04:52.880
Rigzone reported. Iraq and Kazakhstan
both want higher capacity assessments,

88
00:04:52.920 --> 00:04:56.160
and a rollover would push those
fights past Sunday's meeting.

89
00:04:56.400 --> 00:04:57.600
Nothing has been decided.

90
00:04:58.240 --> 00:05:01.920
Equinor has cut its growth guidance
for this year to about three percent,

91
00:05:02.040 --> 00:05:05.840
from four. Bacalhau was shut
in after a dropped object,

92
00:05:05.920 --> 00:05:10.400
Visund is offline after a fire, and
Johan Castberg is at minimum rates

93
00:05:10.480 --> 00:05:13.480
because of offloading problems,
according to World Oil.

94
00:05:13.840 --> 00:05:17.920
In Libya, two Libyan National Army
officers wounded in the Benghazi strike

95
00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:20.320
on the twenty-second
of November have died,

96
00:05:20.360 --> 00:05:22.160
and the army has vowed retaliation.

97
00:05:22.720 --> 00:05:25.280
No restart at the Sharara
field has been reported.

98
00:05:25.840 --> 00:05:29.840
In transatlantic gasoline, Houston
is now the cheapest supply into about

99
00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:34.040
sixty thousand barrels a day of outlets
that used to take European barrels.

100
00:05:34.320 --> 00:05:38.160
Kpler says a December arbitrage
near twenty-two cents a gallon would

101
00:05:38.240 --> 00:05:41.200
let the Amsterdam-Rotterdam-Antwerp
hub compete again.

102
00:05:41.760 --> 00:05:45.360
The chemical tanker Med Emre, carrying
about seven thousand tonnes of

103
00:05:45.440 --> 00:05:47.280
diesel, has sunk off Ibiza.

104
00:05:47.760 --> 00:05:51.000
One seafarer died, Splash
twenty-four seven reported.

105
00:05:51.280 --> 00:05:55.280
And at US pumps, gasoline averaged
about three dollars seventy a gallon

106
00:05:55.360 --> 00:05:56.880
as of the twenty-first of November.

107
00:05:57.360 --> 00:06:00.640
Diesel is still well above that,
according to OilPrice dot com.

108
00:06:01.360 --> 00:06:05.280
What to watch next. Daily European
gas storage readings through to the

109
00:06:05.400 --> 00:06:07.720
third of December, while the cold lasts.

110
00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:12.080
The OPEC plus meeting on Sunday,
including the possible January rollover

111
00:06:12.160 --> 00:06:15.040
and the Iraqi and Kazakh
capacity requests.

112
00:06:15.120 --> 00:06:19.280
And the EIA's weekly report on
